    "scope": "Mapped anchor, signed plan orientation, metric footprint and ground datum.",
    "notes": "Independent main-shaft frame fixes the Park Avenue west-northwest front and 52nd Street south-southwest side. Exact owned parent outline, shaft rectangle and bustle part corroborate the LPC and original MoMA plans; the orthographic capture aligns the main slab and attached rear wings, while the plaza correctly extends toward Park Avenue. Ground Y0 is the lowest local curb; raised plaza and reconstructed street fall are included. Geographic loading and unload passed."
  },
  "fidelityReview": {
    "target": "maximum",
    "status": "passed",
    "scope": "Detailed exterior world-viewer representation with stated reconstruction limits.",
    "notes": "Detailed 157 m exterior accepted for world-viewer use: measured 27 ft 9 in structural bays, 4 ft 7.5 in curtain modules and genuine 4.5 by 6 in bronze I sections, pink-gray glass, 45-degree Venetian blinds, dark louvered crown, open ground columns, Muntz marquee, five-story wings, ten-story bustle and full-height rear spine, travertine lobby enclosures, planted terraces and pink-granite plaza with two pools. Intermediate floor/crown datums, individual blinds, patina, vegetation and curb grade are photographic reconstruction. Temporary sculpture, tenant lettering, flags and moving fountain water are omitted."
  }
